  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri Raj Kumar Dhanuka vs The State Of West Bengal & Anr on 15 February, 2019 Author: Subhasis Dasgupta Bench: Subhasis Dasgupta 22 15.02. Agm 2019 C.R.R. 311 of 2019 Ct 41 Sri Raj Kumar Dhanuka Vs. The State of West Bengal & Anr. Mr. Amlan Jyoti Sengupta, Mr. Chandan Misra, Ms. Sarada Sah, .... For the Petitioner.",
    "facts": "The impugned order dated 18th December, 2018 passed by Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate, Tehatta in G.R. Case No. 572 of 2018 arising out of Karimpur Police Station Case No. 103 of 2018 dated 12th June, 2018, is the subject of assail in this case. By the impugned order, the Trial Court issued warrant of arrest against accused Raj Kumar Dhanuka. From the certified copy of the order of the Trial Court dated 20th December, 2018, it appears that one Bishnu Prosad Kedia, in whose favour the power of attorney was executed by the revisionist empowering him to initiate the prayer for return made such prayer and the Trial Court upon consideration of the entire aspect in the context of report of I.O. returned the seized items upon execution of zimma bond to Bishnu Prosad Kedia, the person in whose favour the power of attorney was executed by the revisionist.",
    "arguments": "According to learned advocate for the revisionist the facts impleading the accused in this case was very much within the knowledge of the Court, and it was considered in its right perspective while making return of the seized items to him.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "According to learned advocate for the revisionist the facts impleading the accused in this case was very much within the knowledge of the Court, and it was considered in its right perspective while making return of the seized items to him.",
